---
import DetailLayout from "../../layouts/DetailLayout.astro";
---

<DetailLayout
  title="Baishuitai Terraces"
  description="Baishuitai Terraces, Shangri-La Yunnan: natural travertine pools called China's Pamukkale. Naxi culture, best season, transport, tickets, and photo tips."
  category="Attraction"
  image="baishuitai-terraces.webp"
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "TouristAttraction",
    "name": "Baishuitai Terraces",
    "description": "Natural travertine terraces near Shangri-La, nicknamed China's Pamukkale. Spring-fed mineral pools cascade down a hillside, best photographed in morning light.",
    "publicAccess": true
  }}
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Baishuitai Terraces</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-500">Natural travertine terraces known as "China's Pamukkale." Spring-fed mineral pools cascade down a hillside in blue and white tiers. A sacred site for the Naxi people and a photographer's dream in morning light.</p>

  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Altitude</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">2,380 m</span></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Time Needed</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">2&ndash;3 hrs</span></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Best Season</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">Mar&ndash;May</span></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Ticket</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">30 RMB</span></div>
  </div>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Overview</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Baishuitai (u767du6c34u53f0) is a stunning natural formation of travertine terraces created over 200,000 years by calcium carbonate-rich spring water flowing down a gentle hillside. The result is a series of brilliant white and pale blue stepped pools that cascade across a slope about 140 meters wide and 50 meters in height. Often called "China's Pamukkale," it predates its more famous Turkish counterpart.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Baishuitai is sacred to the Naxi minority people. According to Naxi legend, the terraces were formed by a deity who taught the Naxi people to grow rice on mountain terraces. It is considered the birthplace of Dongba, the traditional Naxi religion, and Dongba shamans still perform ceremonies here during festivals.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">At 2,380 meters elevation, Baishuitai sits lower than Shangri-La, making it an excellent acclimatization stop if you're driving up from Lijiang (2,400m). The site is compact and easy to explore in 2&ndash;3 hours, with wooden walkways protecting the fragile travertine formations.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">How to Get There</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 space-y-5">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5">
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">From Shangri-La by Car</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Baishuitai is about <strong>100 km</strong> from Shangri-La city (2.5&ndash;3 hours drive). A private car costs <strong>600&ndash;800 RMB</strong> round trip. The road winds through scenic mountain terrain via Tiger Leaping Gorge area, so combining Baishuitai with the gorge in one trip is a smart option.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5">
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900">Bus + Local Transport</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Take a bus from Shangri-La to Sanba Township. From there, a local minibus or shared taxi (20&ndash;30 RMB) takes you 5 km to Baishuitai. This option requires more time and patience but costs under 100 RMB total.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Photography Tips</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span><strong>Morning light</strong> (8:00&ndash;10:00 AM) is best. The low-angle sun makes the pools most reflective and the travertine appears brilliant white.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span>A polarizing filter helps cut glare on the water surfaces for cleaner pool details.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span>The best vantage point is from the upper terraces looking down over the cascading pools.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Food &amp; Where to Eat</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">A small cluster of Naxi family-run restaurants sits at the entrance to Baishuitai, serving simple dishes: Naxi grilled fish (30&ndash;50 RMB), stir-fried vegetables (15&ndash;25 RMB), noodle soup (15 RMB), and local honey tea. The food is simple but authentic. For better dining, combine the visit with lunch at one of the guesthouses near Tiger Leaping Gorge if driving that route.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 p-6">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-emerald-700">Nearby &raquo;</p>
    <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <a href="/attractions/tiger-leaping-gorge/" class="rounded-full bg-white border border-slate-200 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-slate-700 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-700 transition-colors">Tiger Leaping Gorge</a>
      <a href="/attractions/pudacuo-national-park/" class="rounded-full bg-white border border-slate-200 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-slate-700 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-700 transition-colors">Pudacuo National Park</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</DetailLayout>